WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.590
The heroes of Avengers: Infinity War aren't
set to converge on the silver screen until

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:05.590
April 27th.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:10.290
However, as part of the movie's marketing
run, Marvel Studios will be showing the first

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:15.230
30 minutes of Avengers: Infinity War to critics,
fans, and general press over the next couple

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:16.230
of weeks.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:20.140
One such screening took place in London on
Thursday, April 5th, and it gave the world

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.830
the first reaction to the film.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.980
Digital Spy Film staff were lucky enough to
catch the half hour of footage, posting their

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.660
thoughts about it on Twitter:

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.089
"We've just seen 30 minutes of Avengers: Infinity
War.

00:00:30.089 --> 00:00:34.090
Can't say too much but it's way ambitious,
it'll switch tones between different groups

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:38.600
(the Guardians sequence had a very different,
look, feel, and soundtrack to the New York

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.440
scenes), and it's going to be funny.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.620
Still no Hawkeye!"

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.390
It's obvious from the film's eye-popping trailers
and the various television spots that have

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:49.460
aired that the film's cast will, indeed, be
sliced and diced into groups.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:53.309
There's the Battle of New York squad that
consists of Iron Man, Hulk, Doctor Strange,

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:57.469
and Wong, plus Peter Parker, who teams up
with them later in his Iron Spider suit.

00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:02.010
Captain America collaborates with his Nomads
group that includes Falcon, Bucky Barnes,

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:06.760
Black Widow, Black Panther, and Okoye — with
the potential for Vision and Scarlet Witch

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.840
to meet up with the team later as well.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.680
Then we've got Thor meeting the Guardians
of the Galaxy, of course.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.260
"Who the hell are you guys?"

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:19.690
The mention of tonal shifts in this evaluation
of Avengers: Infinity War also lines up with

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.260
something composer Alan Silvestri once said.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:26.760
The movie will feature quick turns in style,
with the music changing to match each mood.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:31.180
Just a few days before the first film reaction
surfaced, Silvestri told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:35.500
"I wrapped Infinity War yesterday, and it
was a really different experience than anything

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:40.140
I'd done before, especially in regard to the
approach and balancing quick shifts in tone."

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:44.540
It also appears that screenwriters Christopher
Markus and Stephen McFeely took some of the

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:49.190
humor that made Captain America: Civil War
such a standout entry in the MCU and infused

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:51.460
it into the Avengers: Infinity War story.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:56.520
"Doctor Strange…" "Oh, we're using our made
up names? Then I'm Spider-Man."

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.220
The only downside to this whole thing?

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:03.030
Jeremy Renner's Hawkeye is still missing,
even 30 minutes into Avengers: Infinity War.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.670
Maybe he'll make an epic entrance in the second
or third act?

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.190
We can only wait to find out.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:08.190
Thanks for watching!

